    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116-a3">

                <pb facs="0209" n="101" xml:id="pg101"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    130.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Notice of the captain of the port.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic">November 2,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the Italian consul:</hi></p>
                <p>There being absolute necessity for the immediate withdrawal of the ships of your
                    nationality from the neighborhood of the islands of Mocangue and Viauna and
                    others situated near the Ponte d’Areia and Toque Toque, I have to ask you to
                    take the necessary measures that such ships may leave as soon as possible the
                    anchorages in which they lie. I take this opportunity to inform you, as is my
                    duty, that the Government of the United States of Brazil does not deem itself
                    bound to give compensation for any loss that such ships may suffer through being
                    in range of the artillery on land.</p>
                <p>I take the opportunity, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">José Pinto do Suz</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Captain of the Port.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
